  "body": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"csrf-token\" content=\"<redacted>\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 16 16'%3E%3Crect width='16' height='16' rx='3' fill='%23141518'/%3E%3Crect x='5' y='5' width='6' height='6' rx='1' fill='%232dd4bf'/%3E%3C/svg%3E\">\n<title>Detection 952 · gitcorpus</title>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  try {\n    var stored = window.localStorage.getItem(\"gc-theme\");\n    if (stored === \"light\" || stored === \"dark\") {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", stored);\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    document.documentElement.removeAttribute(\"data-theme\");\n  }\n})();\n</script>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/app.css\">\n<script src=\"/static/htmx.min.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/rownav.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/applib.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/errors.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/recentfilters.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/modalfocus.js\" defer></script>\n<script src=\"/static/app.js\" defer></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#content\">Skip to content</a>\n<div id=\"nav-progress\" class=\"nav-progress\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n<header class=\"site-header\">\n  <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\">gitcorpus</a>\n  \n  <nav id=\"main-nav\" class=\"site-nav\" aria-label=\"Primary\">\n    <a href=\"/\">Home</a>\n    <a href=\"/runs\">Searches</a>\n    <a href=\"/corpora\">Corpora</a>\n    <a href=\"/filters\">Library</a>\n    <a href=\"/system\">System</a>\n    <a href=\"/detections\" aria-current=\"page\">Detections</a>\n  </nav>\n  <a class=\"status-link\" href=\"/system\" aria-label=\"System status\"><span hx-get=\"/partials/status-dot\" hx-trigger=\"load, every 30s\" hx-swap=\"outerHTML\"></span></a>\n  <button id=\"shortcuts-open\" class=\"button ghost\" type=\"button\" data-open=\"shortcuts-modal\" aria-label=\"Keyboard shortcuts\" title=\"Keyboard shortcuts (?)\">?</button>\n  <button id=\"theme-toggle\" class=\"button ghost\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Toggle dark mode\" title=\"Toggle dark mode\">Theme</button>\n</header>\n<main id=\"content\" class=\"content\">\n\n\n<section class=\"panel\" id=\"run-header\" data-run-id=\"952\">\n  <div class=\"panel-head\">\n    <h1>Detection #1 — search #931</h1>\n    <span class=\"run-hash-wrap\"><span class=\"mono\" data-hash=\"golden-detect\">golden-d</span></span>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"detect-status\" aria-live=\"polite\" data-status=\"done\">\n  <div class=\"run-status-line\">\n    <span class=\"pill done\" data-status=\"done\">Finished</span>\n    \n    \n  </div>\n  \n  \n</div>\n  <p class=\"muted\" id=\"run-elapsed\">Time elapsed: —</p>\n  \n  <details id=\"run-timestamps\">\n    <summary>Technical details</summary>\n    <div class=\"run-meta\">\n      <span id=\"run-id\" data-field=\"run\">run 952</span>\n      <span id=\"run-source\" data-field=\"source\">source api</span>\n      <span id=\"run-created\" data-field=\"created\">created 2026-01-02T00:06:00Z</span>\n      <span id=\"run-started\" data-field=\"started\">started —</span>\n      <span id=\"run-finished\" data-field=\"finished\">finished 2026-01-02T00:07:00Z</span>\n      <span id=\"run-duration\" data-field=\"duration\">duration —</span>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"panel\" id=\"detection-summary\">\n  <div class=\"panel-head\"><h2>Summary</h2></div>\n  <div class=\"cards\">\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <details class=\"info-pop\">\n        <summary aria-label=\"What repos scanned means\">i</summary>\n        <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n          <p>Repos from search #931’s frozen result list that this run processed — every item unless a top-N limit was set.</p>\n          <p>Membership is frozen at search time; signal content is fetched live per repo at detection time. Repos the API could not read are counted as unavailable, never dropped.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n      <h3>Repos scanned</h3><p>1</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <details class=\"info-pop\">\n        <summary aria-label=\"What with any signal means\">i</summary>\n        <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n          <p>Scanned repos with at least one piece of evidence for a selected agent, in any selected channel.</p>\n          <p>This counts repos, not signals — a repo with 200 trailer hits still counts once here. The per-agent totals below show where the evidence lands.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n      <h3>With any signal</h3><p>1</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <details class=\"info-pop\">\n        <summary aria-label=\"What unavailable means\">i</summary>\n        <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n          <p>Repos the GitHub API could not read during the run: deleted or renamed (404), private without access, or a transport/GraphQL failure that survived retries.</p>\n          <p>They contribute no evidence and are never presented as clean. Resume the run to pick them up; the count also appears in the run summary.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n      <h3>Unavailable</h3><p>0</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <details class=\"info-pop\">\n        <summary aria-label=\"What the windowed commit ratio means\">i</summary>\n        <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n          <p>“How much of this repo’s recent work was written with a coding agent?” For each repo we look at the latest 100 commits on its default branch, and count a commit as agent-assisted when its author, its message (an agent co-author or signature line), or the pull request behind it points to a detected agent.</p>\n          <p>Example: a repo where 12 of its counted commits are flagged shows 12%. The number on this card pools every repo in the run — all flagged commits ÷ all counted commits — so repos with more commits count more; it is not the average of the per-repo percentages.</p>\n          <p>Housekeeping commits (merges, reverts, version bumps) and CI bots are skipped on both sides, and only the latest 100 commits are seen: older history and quietly-used agents stay invisible, so treat this as a conservative lower bound.</p>\n          <p>Levels used by the papers: experimental &lt;1% · limited 1–5% · consistent 5–20% · pervasive &gt;20%.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n      <h3>Windowed commit ratio</h3><p>100.0% <span class=\"muted\">pervasive</span></p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <details class=\"info-pop\">\n        <summary aria-label=\"What first signal means\">i</summary>\n        <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n          <p>The earliest date in the window with agent-attributed evidence: the committed date of the oldest matched commit, or the creation date of the oldest matched PR.</p>\n          <p>Because it comes from the 100-commit and most-recent 100-PR windows, it is a lower bound — real adoption may predate it. Full-history dating is the clone tier.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n      <h3>First signal</h3><p>2026-01-02 00:00 UTC</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n  \n  <div id=\"detection-agents\" class=\"run-counts\">\n    <span class=\"count\">Codex <strong>1</strong></span><span class=\"count\">Claude Code <strong>1</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  \n  \n  <p class=\"muted\">Depth: 100 commits · 100 PRs · 100 issues (windowed). Papers’ baseline: ~0.5–1% false positives, ~3% borderline; detection is an undercount. Hover or tap the ⓘ on any card for details.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"panel\" id=\"detection-evidence\">\n  <div class=\"panel-head\">\n    <h2>Per-repo evidence</h2>\n    <div class=\"form-actions\">\n      \n      <form method=\"get\" action=\"/runs/952/export\" class=\"export-group\">\n        <select class=\"field-input\" name=\"format\" id=\"detection-export-evidence-format\" aria-label=\"Evidence export format\">\n          <option value=\"detections\">CSV — one row per evidence item</option>\n          <option value=\"detections-json\">JSON — one object per evidence item</option>\n        </select>\n        <button class=\"button\" type=\"submit\" id=\"detection-export-evidence\">Export evidence</button>\n        <details class=\"info-pop\">\n          <summary aria-label=\"What the evidence export contains\">i</summary>\n          <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n            <p>This file carries every stored evidence row for the run — agent, channel, and the commit, path, or PR details — with the raw evidence JSON, regenerated live from the database so nothing is capped by Excel's row limit.</p>\n            <p>CSV is a flat table for spreadsheets; JSON preserves the nested evidence objects (and carries the exact detected-at moment). CSV cells that start with a formula character (= + -) are quoted with a leading apostrophe so spreadsheets show the literal text.</p>\n          </div>\n        </details>\n      </form>\n      <form method=\"get\" action=\"/runs/952/export\" class=\"export-group\">\n        <select class=\"field-input\" name=\"format\" id=\"detection-export-run-format\" aria-label=\"Repos export format\">\n          <option value=\"csv\">CSV — one row per scanned repo</option>\n          <option value=\"json\">JSON — repos with detection rollup</option>\n        </select>\n        <button class=\"button\" type=\"submit\" id=\"detection-export-run\">Export repos</button>\n        <details class=\"info-pop\">\n          <summary aria-label=\"What the repos export contains\">i</summary>\n          <div class=\"info-pop-body\">\n            <p>One row per scanned repo in CSV, one object per repo in JSON — the corpus fields plus a detection rollup: agents, adoption level, commit ratio, and per-channel evidence counts.</p>\n            <p>Repo metadata the detection run did not carry (language, license, stars date, geography) is filled from the stored repo records, so the file is complete for joining. Use it to join detection results back onto the search corpus. CSV and JSON hold the same columns; the filenames and the tools that open them differ.</p>\n          </div>\n        </details>\n      </form>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n  \n  <form id=\"detection-filters\" class=\"filter-row\" method=\"get\" action=\"/detections/952\">\n    <label class=\"field\" for=\"detection-filter-signal\">\n      <span class=\"field-label\">Has signal</span>\n      <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"detection-filter-signal\" name=\"signal\" value=\"1\">\n    </label>\n    <label class=\"field\" for=\"detection-filter-agent\">\n      <span class=\"field-label\">Agent</span>\n      <select class=\"field-input\" id=\"detection-filter-agent\" name=\"agent\">\n        <option value=\"\">All agents</option>\n        <option value=\"Claude Code\">Claude Code</option><option value=\"Codex\">Codex</option>\n      </select>\n    </label>\n    <label class=\"field\" for=\"detection-filter-channel\">\n      <span class=\"field-label\">Channel</span>\n      <select class=\"field-input\" id=\"detection-filter-channel\" name=\"channel\">\n        <option value=\"\">All channels</option>\n        <option value=\"file\">file</option><option value=\"pr_metadata\">pr_metadata</option>\n      </select>\n    </label>\n    <div class=\"field filter-submit\">\n      <span class=\"field-label\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&nbsp;</span>\n      <button class=\"button\" type=\"submit\" id=\"detection-filter-apply\">Filter</button>\n    </div>\n  </form>\n  \n  <details class=\"evidence-repo\" id=\"detection-repo-911\">\n    <summary>octo/alpha · Claude Code</summary>\n    <div class=\"evidence-body\">\n      \n      \n        \n        <div class=\"evidence-channel\" data-channel=\"file\">\n          <h4>file</h4>\n          <ul>\n            <li data-agent=\"Claude Code\"><strong>Claude Code</strong> — CLAUDE.md</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n        \n      \n        \n        <div class=\"evidence-channel\" data-channel=\"pr_metadata\">\n          <h4>pr_metadata</h4>\n          <ul>\n            <li data-agent=\"Codex\"><strong>Codex</strong> — PR #7 → commit a1</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n        \n      \n    </div>\n  </details>\n  \n  \n  \n</section>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n  var form = document.getElementById(\"detection-filters\");\n  if (!form) {\n    return;\n  }\n  form.addEventListener(\"change\", function () {\n    form.submit();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n\n\n</main>\n<div id=\"shortcuts-modal\" class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-labelledby=\"shortcuts-title\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"modal-panel\" role=\"document\">\n    <div class=\"panel-head\">\n      <h2 id=\"shortcuts-title\">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>\n      <button id=\"shortcuts-close\" class=\"button ghost\" type=\"button\" data-close=\"shortcuts-modal\" aria-label=\"Close shortcuts\">Close</button>\n    </div>\n    <table class=\"data-table shortcuts-table\">\n      <caption class=\"sr-only\">Keyboard shortcuts</caption>\n      <thead>\n        <tr><th scope=\"col\">Key</th><th scope=\"col\">Action</th></tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"g-h\"><td><kbd>g</kbd> then <kbd>h</kbd></td><td>Go home</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"g-f\"><td><kbd>g</kbd> then <kbd>f</kbd></td><td>Go to Find</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"g-r\"><td><kbd>g</kbd> then <kbd>r</kbd></td><td>Go to Runs</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"g-l\"><td><kbd>g</kbd> then <kbd>l</kbd></td><td>Go to Library (filters)</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"j\"><td><kbd>j</kbd></td><td>Select next row</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"k\"><td><kbd>k</kbd></td><td>Select previous row</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"enter\"><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Open selected row</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"escape\"><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>Close this help or a dialog</td></tr>\n        <tr data-shortcut=\"question\"><td><kbd>?</kbd></td><td>Toggle this help</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toast\" class=\"toast\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" hidden></div>\n</body>\n</html>"
}
